# 🧩 d. Modular API Development

**Modular development** means dividing an application into separate modules or Django apps based on functionality.

Instead of building everything inside one large application:

```text
project/
└── app/
    ├── models.py
    ├── views.py
    └── serializers.py
```

a larger application can be divided into multiple apps:

```text
project/
│
├── users/
├── products/
├── orders/
├── payments/
└── notifications/
```

Each app handles a specific responsibility.

### Example

```text
users/
├── models.py
├── serializers.py
├── views.py
└── urls.py

products/
├── models.py
├── serializers.py
├── views.py
└── urls.py

orders/
├── models.py
├── serializers.py
├── views.py
└── urls.py
```

### Benefits

- Clear separation of responsibilities
- Easier development
- Easier testing
- Easier maintenance
- Better team collaboration
- Individual modules can evolve independently

